\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Circuit-breaker interpretability and onset-rate boundaries across three real telemetry regimes (pink shading and dotted line mark fault span and onset $t^*$). Row\nobreakspace  {}1 shows continuous sensor traces; Row\nobreakspace  {}2 stacks active breakers across short ($S_1{=}16$), medium ($S_2{=}32$), long ($S_3{=}64$), and drift ($|\bar  {e}_c|$) groups summing directly to $N_{128}(\tau )$ against $K_{\text  {Lite}}$; Row\nobreakspace  {}3 plots score-to-threshold ratios (alarming above $1{\times }$). \textbf  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}Abrupt chemical spike (\texttt  {GECCO}): all four breaker groups surge together to $4.9{\times }$ $K_{\text  {Lite}}$ ($60/128$ dials) while 1D SPOT barely reaches $1.04{\times }$. \textbf  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}In-range contextual anomaly (\texttt  {SMAP A-7}): telemetry stays within $\pm 2.5\sigma $ as oscillation frequency shifts, stacking $S_2, S_3$ and drift into a sustained plateau up to $1.84{\times }$ $K_{\text  {Lite}}$ (vs.\ $1.25{\times }$ on 1D SPOT). \textbf  {(c)}\nobreakspace  {}Slow thermal ramp (\texttt  {GHL-44}): temperature climbs linearly over $860$ steps with $N_{128}=0 < K_{\text  {Lite}}$ until the late reset, whereas frozen-reference drift crosses $1{\times }$ inside the ramp.}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:panel_interpretability}{{4}{11}{Circuit-breaker interpretability and onset-rate boundaries across three real telemetry regimes (pink shading and dotted line mark fault span and onset $t^*$). Row~1 shows continuous sensor traces; Row~2 stacks active breakers across short ($S_1{=}16$), medium ($S_2{=}32$), long ($S_3{=}64$), and drift ($|\bar {e}_c|$) groups summing directly to $N_{128}(\tau )$ against $K_{\text {Lite}}$; Row~3 plots score-to-threshold ratios (alarming above $1{\times }$). \textbf {(a)}~Abrupt chemical spike (\texttt {GECCO}): all four breaker groups surge together to $4.9{\times }$ $K_{\text {Lite}}$ ($60/128$ dials) while 1D SPOT barely reaches $1.04{\times }$. \textbf {(b)}~In-range contextual anomaly (\texttt {SMAP A-7}): telemetry stays within $\pm 2.5\sigma $ as oscillation frequency shifts, stacking $S_2, S_3$ and drift into a sustained plateau up to $1.84{\times }$ $K_{\text {Lite}}$ (vs.\ $1.25{\times }$ on 1D SPOT). \textbf {(c)}~Slow thermal ramp (\texttt {GHL-44}): temperature climbs linearly over $860$ steps with $N_{128}=0 < K_{\text {Lite}}$ until the late reset, whereas frozen-reference drift crosses $1{\times }$ inside the ramp}{figure.4}{}}
